event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":83,"item_id":"rs_0422ee0e8509ffde016aca202c5c7c81948576101931a565f5","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering test structures**\n\nI’m thinking about how to manage tests effectively. It seems like I can append new tests inside the existing ones, keeping the detailed comparisons intact. This way, none of the tests would fail even if I insert additional ones. I might need to create my own tests or enhance existing ones after the initial restart. It’s all about maintaining clarity and proper assertions in my tasks and the restart process."}

